# HW-021a - the ESP32 I2S mem-slab leak, on STOCK Zephyr. 2026-07-12, COM35.
#
# 100 reconfigure/START/DROP cycles with a census of the TX and RX slabs before each.
# The slab drains by EXACTLY ONE BLOCK PER DIRECTION PER CYCLE and is empty by the 8th.
# It does not fail: i2s_buf_write() allocates with K_FOREVER, so an exhausted slab is a
# silent unkillable block. The guard in the test is what turns that into a report.
